--- Check 3: Port 6432 listening ---
$ ss -tlnp | grep 6432
LISTEN 0      128          0.0.0.0:6432      0.0.0.0:*

Port 6432 is listening on all interfaces.

--- Check 4: pgbouncer config ---
$ cat /etc/pgbouncer/pgbouncer.ini
[databases]
quantdb = host=127.0.0.1 port=5432 dbname=quantdb

[pgbouncer]
listen_addr = 0.0.0.0
listen_port = 6432
auth_type = scram-sha-256
auth_file = /etc/pgbouncer/userlist.txt
pool_mode = transaction
default_pool_size = 50
max_client_conn = 1000
max_db_connections = 100
log_connections = 1
log_disconnections = 1
log_pooler_errors = 1
stats_period = 60
admin_users = pgbouncer

Config looks solid: transaction pooling, SCRAM auth, 50 pool size, 1000 max clients.

